# code snips: How the pieces connect
Frontend (Vite/Vue): it calls the backend at VITE_API_URL, read in gallery.ts. Vite inlines this value at build time.
Backend (Next.js api-server): it allows only one browser origin, set by CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGIN in cors.ts. It falls back to http://localhost:5173, so if you don't set it in production the browser will block your site.
Setup
1. Backend (your running server, or a second Vercel project with Root Directory api-server). Set these server-side variables:

Variable	Value
CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME	your cloud name
CLOUDINARY_API_KEY	your API key
CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET	your API secret
CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGIN	exact frontend origin, e.g. https://yourdomain.com (no trailing slash, no path)
If it's a self-hosted server, set these as environment variables, then rebuild and restart it. It must be served over HTTPS, otherwise browsers block the calls from your HTTPS site.

2. Frontend (Vercel project, root directory = repo root). Set this variable:

Variable	Value
VITE_API_URL	backend base URL, e.g. https://api.yourdomain.com (no trailing slash)
3. Redeploy the frontend after setting VITE_API_URL. It's baked in at build time, so changing it without redeploying has no effect.

4. Check it. Run this from the repo root:


